**Root cause:** trigger-level YAML schema doesn't accept `options` as a direct field when using `filename:` (repo-hosted `cloudbuild.yaml`) — worker pool assignment for this trigger type goes through a dedicated flag instead, not the exported YAML structure.

**Correct fix — use `update` with `--worker-pool` flag directly:**

```bash
gcloud beta builds triggers update careernavigator-backend-staging \
  --project=pg-ae-n-app-125609 \
  --region=me-central2 \
  --worker-pool=projects/pg-ae-n-app-125609/locations/me-central2/workerPools/cn-backend-private-pool
```

**Verify:**
```bash
gcloud beta builds triggers export careernavigator-backend-staging \
  --project=pg-ae-n-app-125609 \
  --region=me-central2 \
  --destination=trigger-backend-verify.yaml

cat trigger-backend-verify.yaml
```
Look for `options.pool.name` (or similar) now present in the export — schema should accept it now since it's coming from the proper API field, not raw YAML import.

**Then test:**
```bash
gcloud builds triggers run careernavigator-backend-staging \
  --project=pg-ae-n-app-125609 \
  --region=me-central2 \
  --branch=staging
```

